<%#
  Shown when an admin adds a payment to an order from the backend.

  There is deliberately no card form here. A Square charge needs a token from
  the Web Payments SDK running in the customer's browser; an admin typing a card
  number into this page would mean card data hitting our server, which CLAUDE.md
  forbids outright.

  So this explains the supported routes instead of offering a form that could
  not work.
%>
<div class="square-admin-source">
  <p>
    <strong>Card payments are taken through the customer's checkout.</strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    Square requires the card to be entered in the customer's own browser, so a
    card cannot be keyed in here. To charge this customer, either:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>ask them to complete checkout in the portal, or</li>
    <li>take the payment in the Square dashboard or Square app, then record it
      against this order using the <em>Check</em> payment method with the Square
      receipt number in the notes.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <small>Refunds for card payments taken through the portal can be issued from
    the Payments tab, and will be sent to Square.</small>
  </p>
</div>
